[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'fal Sandbox gives you the ability to&nbsp; test multiple different models from&nbsp;&nbsp; the same text prompt. This allows you to test&nbsp; multiple models at once, compare the outputs,&nbsp;&nbsp; understand how much each model costs, and roughly&nbsp; how long each one takes to process. In this video,&nbsp;&nbsp; I\'m going to walk you through the basics&nbsp; of using fal Sandbox. Let\'s get started.'

[00:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'To get to fal Sandbox, head to the website and&nbsp; up to generate. and it\'s our first thing under&nbsp;&nbsp; the generate tab here. So, welcome to sandbox.&nbsp; You\'ll see obviously a gallery of some images that&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I\'ve generated in the past. But let\'s direct our&nbsp; attention down here to the simple input box. So,&nbsp;&nbsp; this is your pretty standard prompt box. And I\'m&nbsp; just going to make up a prompt right now quickly.&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'And the prompt is a Korean girl in her 20s on&nbsp; her iPhone in San Francisco at sunset. How how&nbsp;&nbsp; romantic. There\'s a couple things going on here&nbsp; that we want to point out before we send this&nbsp;&nbsp; off. First is aspect ratio. So, I\'m going to make&nbsp; it 16x9 like a film. And we\'ll notice that we\'re&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'in text to image mode. So, we can um expect some&nbsp; images coming back. And before we send this off,&nbsp;&nbsp; we want to look at the sets of models that we\'re&nbsp; going to be testing. And by default, I believe&nbsp;&nbsp; we\'re using uh the state-of-the-art models right&nbsp; here. So, that\'s going to be Krea, uh GPT Image 2,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Gro Imagine, and Flux 2 Pro. So, just for fun,&nbsp; let\'s go ahead and send this off. And it does&nbsp;&nbsp; say that this is roughly going to cost about 27.&nbsp; I\'m going to send this off and then we\'ll look at&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the results. So our very first sandbox generation&nbsp; has finished here and let\'s kind of analyze what&nbsp;&nbsp; happened. Again, we saw while this is generating&nbsp; that Grok imagine was the fastest to process. It&nbsp;&nbsp; took 5.8 seconds and roughly 2 cents I think. Next&nbsp; was Flux 2 Pro at 8.9 seconds at 3 cents. And then&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Korea version 28 seconds. So quite a bit longer at&nbsp; 6 cents. And then we have our most expensive and&nbsp;&nbsp; longest generating and honestly one of my again&nbsp; my favorite models is GPT image 2.0 118 seconds&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'so almost 2 minutes and um 10 cents. So this&nbsp; is important information as you start building&nbsp;&nbsp; uh gen media systems at scale that you might want&nbsp; to consider that oh GPT takes a very long time.&nbsp;&nbsp;'

